**All three are the SAME guard-weakening shape on three different fields**, and all three permit reachable stores of uninitialised `buf` -- *the exact defect class `#519` exists to close.*  M13 and M14 were treated as floor kills and justified a forty-row expansion.  **The only thing separating M28 from them is which rows happen to exist to see it** -- and in the seat's words, *"an instrument-relative escape is not a contract-relative exemption."*

*** AND THIS PROJECT'S OWN CLASS-CLOSURE AMENDMENT FIRES ON EXACTLY THIS PATTERN. ***  It says: *when two consecutive passes find breaches of ONE CLASS, the next repair owes the CLASS CLOSURE -- enumerate the full space and close every cell in ONE diff, rather than buying cells one at a time.*  Pass 1 found M13/M14; pass 2 found M28; **same class, consecutive passes.**  The amendment exists precisely so a round stops repairing the cell it was shown and closes the space -- which is what the measuring seat did for `{tlb_mode} x {bufdepth}` and what I was about to NOT do for `color_mode`.

**THE COST IS ELEVEN ROWS, NOT ONE AND NOT 192.**  Single-axis predicates over all three fields close with the sixteen `(tlb, depth)` cells already shipped at nibble `0xf0`, PLUS the twelve reaching nibbles at ONE cell -- of which one is already rowed.  **Eleven new readbacks at an existing cell.**  My brief's "4 x 4 x 12" was a wrong scare in one direction and grok's "one row" is a cell repair rather than a closure in the other; *neither number was the closure, and the closure is the thing the rule asks for.*

**REVISED RE-TABLE: +11 (`color_mode` closure), +1 (`(1,0)` address), -4 (`ann cum`) = 67 rows.**

*** MY DISPOSITION CHANGES: `M28` IS NOT CLAUSE-(e) DEBT.  It is the second pass of a recurring class, and the round owes the closure before it ships. ***  The rule question for the flagship seat stands and is now sharper -- it is no longer *is M28 in or out*, but **does the body-tested- partition bound survive the symmetry argument at all**, given that `bufdepth` and `color_mode` weaken the same guard in the same way.

*Recorded against my own earlier entry in this row, which said one row and clause (e).  Three seats gave three different answers -- clause (e), floor breach on the operand-swap route, and floor breach on the symmetry route -- and the third is the one that cites this project's own governing amendment.  Count the arguments, not the seats.*

*** PASS 2, MEASURED: **FLOOR BREACH.**  SIX MUTANTS SCORE 59/59 ON THE SHIPPED INSTRUMENT AND EVERY ONE WRITES UNINITIALISED HOST STACK INTO GUEST MEMORY.  `#519` DOES NOT CLOSE ON THIS DETECTOR. ***  13 builds, 11 instrument runs, 13 controls; `regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/`.

    M30_tilenrdecline   ok=0 -> if (tile_nr == 0) ok = 0;        59/59   tile 1, 0x70630000
