    M37_fgvalue         ok=0 -> if (*color == 0xaabbccdd) ok=0;  59/59   fg 0x12345678

*** `0x6368696e` IS ASCII **"chin"** -- host stack TEXT reaching guest-visible memory. ***

**THE SMALLEST IS ELEVEN CHARACTERS: `if (ok)` -> `if (ok || tile_nr)`.**

**THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS PROVE THE FINDING IS SPECIFIC, NOT 'the probe ignores geometry':** `if (ok || ofs)`, `|| x` and `|| y` each score **58/59**, killed by exactly one row -- `ycrcb x4y1`.  **That row works.**  It simply cannot reach the tile INDEX: its cell is LINEAR at (4,1) where `x >> 12 == 0`, and a tiled (4,1) would not have helped either since `x / tilewidth == 0` at every bufdepth.  Each mutant moved exactly one control cell and all four liveness/attribution rows were invariant across all 11 legs, so every write is attributable.

*** SEVERITY, AND IT INVERTS THE USUAL PICTURE: at 32bpp a tile is 128x128, so `tile_nr == 0` is `x < 128 && y < 128`.  On the default 1280x1024 framebuffer M30 KEEPS the fix over **1.25% of the screen and RE-OPENS IT OVER THE OTHER 98.75%** -- and all 59 rows sit inside the 1.25%. ***

**AND THE WRONG WARRANT I RECORDED THIS MORNING WAS ALREADY REUSED, WHICH IS EXACTLY WHY THIS PROJECT CORRECTS REASONS AND NOT ONLY CONCLUSIONS.**  The flow test was applied CORRECTLY to `tlb_mode` (floor axis, via `tileptr`) and then **stopped at the ARRAY and never reached the INDEX**: `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16`, so `tile_nr` flows into the guarded body's ADDRESS operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does -- and `#100` in this same function already calls `tile_nr` guest-derived and bounds it.  `ofs`'s own formula `512*y + (x % tilewidth) * bufdepth` contains x and y, while my PRETABLE named only `tlb_mode` and `bufdepth` as its dependencies.

**QUESTION 2's SENTENCE IS TRUE AND THE WORD DOING ALL THE WORK IS 'ALONE'.**  Of the four body-read lvalues, `bufdepth` is closed over its domain and `buf` over its label partition -- **`tileptr`'s INDEX and `ofs` are each held at a SINGLE VALUE by all 59 rows.**

*** THIS IS THE THIRD CONSECUTIVE PASS FINDING THE SAME SHAPE (bufdepth/linear, then color_mode, now tile index/y/fg), SO THE CLASS-CLOSURE RULE BITES HARD: the next repair owes the closure in ONE DIFF, not another cell. ***  The 16-cell closure was principled and **incomplete on its own principle** -- the same reasoning that justified closing `tlb_mode x bufdepth` justifies closing the tile index.  *Reachability is a `sw` to `DE_MODE_DST`, not a driver design choice, so the "guests do not traverse this space" objection fails too.*

*** 2026-09-11 PASS 2 / CLASS CLOSURE (Opus 5, `/tmp/gxop519p2`).  **THE CLASS CLOSURE LANDED IN ONE DIFF: 59 -> 77 ROWS, BASE 77/77, AND ALL SIX 59/59 ESCAPES DIE.** ***

    M30 74/77   M31 74/77   M32 75/77   M33 75/77   M37 67/77   M28 67/77

**The enumeration is BOUNDED and that is why this is not `#392`:** the guarded store reads `tileptr`, `ofs`, `buf`, `bufdepth`, and **`tile_nr`, `tile_nr_x`, `tile_nr_y`, `xofs` and `ofs` are not independent axes** -- each is a pure function of `(x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode)`, the latter two already closed by table 3.  So *close every derived coordinate* IS *close the pair (x, y)*: **two free variables, read off the function, unable to grow by argument.**

**MY ELEVEN-ROW COSTING WAS ONE TOO MANY.**  Twelve nibbles reach `default:` and **two were already driven** (`0xf0` and `0x50`, at the same cell), so ten.  The `*color` axis costs **zero** extra rows because the nibbles are drawn in a second foreground colour.

Four coordinate cells, each in its own tile so every accept is a clause-(f) anchor at a distinct physical address: C1 (132,0) C2 (0,1) C3 (0,128) **C4 (132,129) -- THE JOINT CELL**, where the pairwise disjunctions are true everywhere else.  `x = 132` not 128 because at 128 `x % tilewidth` is 0 and `xofs` stays pinned; `y = 129` not 128 because `y &= 127` runs before the colour switch.  **11 of 12 predictions exact, including `M41` reddening ONLY C4** -- the joint cell's entire warrant, measured.

**`silent` IS JUSTIFIED BY MEASUREMENT, NOT JUDGEMENT:** `M38_acceptannounce` reds the four `silent` rows and **zero** `ann1` rows.  The four `ann cum` rows are deleted -- their kill sets were strict subsets.

*** AND A READ-ONLY AUDIT OF THE SEAT'S OWN BLOCK FOUND REAL DEFECTS IN IT, WHICH IS THE PART WORTH KEEPING: ***
* **The word "complete" did not belong in the enumeration.**  The TLB array's *contents* were named as an input to `tileptr` and then dropped from the conclusion.  `tileptr` is the store's address operand, so by the same flow test that makes `tlb_mode` a floor axis, **the array VALUE is a genuine floor-shaped gap** -- `if (ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000))` is predicted 77/77.  **Filed as OWED, not fixed, because a repair owes its own pass.**
* `mode & 1`, `x & 1`, `y & 2` also sweep -- **within-class value slices, not closable by any finite row set.**  The contract is rewritten to separate **EXHAUSTED** axes (`tlb_mode`, `bufdepth`, `color_mode`) from **SAMPLED** ones, rather than calling all of them closed.
* **L4, corrected in place:** a probe comment claimed every row held `xofs` at zero; it is 16 at `ycrcb x4y1`.
* One audit claim was CHECKED AND REJECTED -- table 3's latch mutants are carried forward, in the regression tail.

STILL OWED: the 25-leg regression tail is live for score comparability; the clone holds its sentinel until its two-part clearance.  **Gate wiring is OWED, not exempt** -- `gate_arm.sh:1283` already runs the sibling probe on the same machine -- **and it must pin 77, not 59.**

TWO RESIDUALS, both READINGS not measurements (`killtable4_20260911/RESIDUALS.md`): the sibling `tlb_mode` arm has **the same blind spot** (`if (tile_nr) *color = random();` predicted to sweep its 8-row detector), and **the GET-side `default:` has no detector at all** plus an unlatched guest-drivable `fatal()` filed nowhere.

*A method note from the seat, and it is this session's recurring shape: its own "sentinel absent" line was a FALSE NEGATIVE -- it used git-bash `test -f /tmp/...`, and **git-bash `/tmp` and WSL `/tmp` are different filesystems.*

*** 2026-09-11, `M1_reinstate` (clause (b), verbatim reinstatement) -- **THE DELETION WARRANT IS CONFIRMED EMPIRICALLY, NOT BY KILL-SET ANALYSIS ALONE**. ***

    37 - 4 + 16 = 49,  measured 49.

**The clause-(b) mutant lost PRECISELY its four `ann cum` reds and nothing else.**  Those four rows were deleted from the detector on the grounds that their kill sets were strict subsets of other rows' -- an argument from analysis.  *The arithmetic now closes on the measurement*: had the deletion cost any mutant its only kill, the reconciliation would not have balanced.

The 16 gained are exactly the designed set -- the ten `nib` declines, the four `xy dec` cells, and both new announce rows.  *(`M1` restores the old UNLATCHED `fatal()` with different text, so the `ANN` count drops to zero, which is why both announce rows red.)*

**And the five accept anchors plus `xy anchor t0` correctly stayed GREEN**, because `M1` touches only the `default:` arm -- a negative control on the deletion, in the same leg.

*This is the shape the vacuity floor asks for and rarely gets in one number: a row-count change, a predicted kill-set delta, and a measured total that reconciles without slack.*

