186: 
187: > *** BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30`'s `if (tile_nr == 0) ok = 0;` IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT. ***  *My brief demanded closure over selectors the rule does not put inside the floor, which is the `#392` shape wearing the class-closure rule's clothes.  The seat's closing sentence is the one to keep: these additions **'must not be represented as full closure over arbitrary predicates on all function inputs.'***
188: 
189: === THE BOUNDED, REVIEWABLE IMPROVEMENT -- what is actually owed ===
190:   * **eleven missing mode/depth/latch cells**;
191:   * **one reverse-latch assertion** -- one aggregate `colour/others` assertion appended to an EXISTING colour-first session: after the colour announcement, drive the twelve other sites and require each expected announcement.  **Control family `SET_OTHER(j)`: the colour warning update also sets another site's bit**, observable as the missing announcement from site `j`.  *The current other-first sequence stays green under that error because the other bit was already set.*  **One assertion, no new process.**
192:   * **strengthened four depth-eight assertions**;
193:   * an **unconditional default-arm `return`**;
194:   * a **contract that names its ACTUAL partitions**.
195: 
196: *** A CAUTION ON EXTENDING COORDINATES, which would have bitten the obvious implementation: *** *'Reusing C1's fixed vertex at another depth can select another tile; changing only the mode can turn a proposed decline test into an earlier invalid-pointer return.'*  **Each added address/depth setup needs an ACCEPTING control proving that mapping reaches its intended destination** -- otherwise a row that looks like a decline test is really an early-return test.
197: 
198: === `buf[8] = {0}` IS ACCEPTED, BUT NOT AS BELT-AND-BRACES ===
199: **Accepted as a candidate companion repair on a TRANSFERRED WARRANT**: the same file's `#509` comment records the same buffer-to-guest failure mechanism and explicitly leaves other widths outstanding.  **Not a measured delta.**  And it is not free -- *'I would not describe it as merely belt-and-braces'*:
200:   * **it changes six accepted PUT format/depth combinations**;
201:   * at the shared declaration it **also changes GET behaviour when the read supplies fewer bytes than packing consumes**;
202:   * it establishes deterministic bytes, **not hardware-correct semantics** for every unsupported combination;
203:   * its generated-code and performance cost are unmeasured.
204: 
205: *'The permitted files do not establish that zero padding is the intended hardware behavior for all those combinations.  They do establish why copying uninitialized storage is unacceptable.'*
206: 
207: **AND THE TWO ROWS STAY SEPARATE, with the invariants named:** [[sgirandomcolour]] = *an unsupported PUT performs NO STORE*; [[sgirebufuninit]] = *every byte consumed by an actual transfer or colour reconstruction is INITIALIZED*.  **Different invariants, so the distinction survives** -- I had asked whether the six escapes collapse them, and they do not.
208: 
209: **STATUS: `#519` still must not commit as-is** (the escapes are real and the default arm should return unconditionally), **but the round owes a BOUNDED list, not the unbounded closure I specified.**  Landing held by owner ruling.
