*** AND THIS PROJECT'S OWN CLASS-CLOSURE AMENDMENT FIRES ON EXACTLY THIS PATTERN. ***  It says: *when two consecutive passes find breaches of ONE CLASS, the next repair owes the CLASS CLOSURE -- enumerate the full space and close every cell in ONE diff, rather than buying cells one at a time.*  Pass 1 found M13/M14; pass 2 found M28; **same class, consecutive passes.**  The amendment exists precisely so a round stops repairing the cell it was shown and closes the space -- which is what the measuring seat did for `{tlb_mode} x {bufdepth}` and what I was about to NOT do for `color_mode`.

