*** `0x6368696e` IS ASCII **"chin"** -- host stack TEXT reaching guest-visible memory. ***

**THE SMALLEST IS ELEVEN CHARACTERS: `if (ok)` -> `if (ok || tile_nr)`.**

**THE NEGATIVE CONTROLS PROVE THE FINDING IS SPECIFIC, NOT 'the probe ignores geometry':** `if (ok || ofs)`, `|| x` and `|| y` each score **58/59**, killed by exactly one row -- `ycrcb x4y1`.  **That row works.**  It simply cannot reach the tile INDEX: its cell is LINEAR at (4,1) where `x >> 12 == 0`, and a tiled (4,1) would not have helped either since `x / tilewidth == 0` at every bufdepth.  Each mutant moved exactly one control cell and all four liveness/attribution rows were invariant across all 11 legs, so every write is attributable.

*** SEVERITY, AND IT INVERTS THE USUAL PICTURE: at 32bpp a tile is 128x128, so `tile_nr == 0` is `x < 128 && y < 128`.  On the default 1280x1024 framebuffer M30 KEEPS the fix over **1.25% of the screen and RE-OPENS IT OVER THE OTHER 98.75%** -- and all 59 rows sit inside the 1.25%. ***

**AND THE WRONG WARRANT I RECORDED THIS MORNING WAS ALREADY REUSED, WHICH IS EXACTLY WHY THIS PROJECT CORRECTS REASONS AND NOT ONLY CONCLUSIONS.**  The flow test was applied CORRECTLY to `tlb_mode` (floor axis, via `tileptr`) and then **stopped at the ARRAY and never reached the INDEX**: `tileptr = d->re_tlb_a[tile_nr] << 16`, so `tile_nr` flows into the guarded body's ADDRESS operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does -- and `#100` in this same function already calls `tile_nr` guest-derived and bounds it.  `ofs`'s own formula `512*y + (x % tilewidth) * bufdepth` contains x and y, while my PRETABLE named only `tlb_mode` and `bufdepth` as its dependencies.

**QUESTION 2's SENTENCE IS TRUE AND THE WORD DOING ALL THE WORK IS 'ALONE'.**  Of the four body-read lvalues, `bufdepth` is closed over its domain and `buf` over its label partition -- **`tileptr`'s INDEX and `ofs` are each held at a SINGLE VALUE by all 59 rows.**

*** THIS IS THE THIRD CONSECUTIVE PASS FINDING THE SAME SHAPE (bufdepth/linear, then color_mode, now tile index/y/fg), SO THE CLASS-CLOSURE RULE BITES HARD: the next repair owes the closure in ONE DIFF, not another cell. ***  The 16-cell closure was principled and **incomplete on its own principle** -- the same reasoning that justified closing `tlb_mode x bufdepth` justifies closing the tile index.  *Reachability is a `sw` to `DE_MODE_DST`, not a driver design choice, so the "guests do not traverse this space" objection fails too.*

