TWO RESIDUALS, both READINGS not measurements (`killtable4_20260911/RESIDUALS.md`): the sibling `tlb_mode` arm has **the same blind spot** (`if (tile_nr) *color = random();` predicted to sweep its 8-row detector), and **the GET-side `default:` has no detector at all** plus an unlatched guest-drivable `fatal()` filed nowhere.

*A method note from the seat, and it is this session's recurring shape: its own "sentinel absent" line was a FALSE NEGATIVE -- it used git-bash `test -f /tmp/...`, and **git-bash `/tmp` and WSL `/tmp` are different filesystems.*

*** 2026-09-11, `M1_reinstate` (clause (b), verbatim reinstatement) -- **THE DELETION WARRANT IS CONFIRMED EMPIRICALLY, NOT BY KILL-SET ANALYSIS ALONE**. ***

    37 - 4 + 16 = 49,  measured 49.

**The clause-(b) mutant lost PRECISELY its four `ann cum` reds and nothing else.**  Those four rows were deleted from the detector on the grounds that their kill sets were strict subsets of other rows' -- an argument from analysis.  *The arithmetic now closes on the measurement*: had the deletion cost any mutant its only kill, the reconciliation would not have balanced.

The 16 gained are exactly the designed set -- the ten `nib` declines, the four `xy dec` cells, and both new announce rows.  *(`M1` restores the old UNLATCHED `fatal()` with different text, so the `ANN` count drops to zero, which is why both announce rows red.)*

**And the five accept anchors plus `xy anchor t0` correctly stayed GREEN**, because `M1` touches only the `default:` arm -- a negative control on the deletion, in the same leg.

*This is the shape the vacuity floor asks for and rarely gets in one number: a row-count change, a predicted kill-set delta, and a measured total that reconciles without slack.*

*** 2026-09-11 -- **CLAUSES (a) AND (b) DISCHARGED ON THE NEW 77-ROW INSTRUMENT**, by a matched pair rather than by assertion. ***

    M11_null      28/77     (whole-file PRE-FIX dev_sgi_re.c)
    M1_reinstate  28/77     (verbatim reinstatement of the random() arm)

**The two score IDENTICALLY -- as they did on the 59-row instrument, where both scored 22/59.**  That pairing discharges two clauses at once: **(a)** the detector fails on the pre-fix build, and **(b)** it fails on a verbatim reinstatement of the removed defect.

**And both remain well short of clean, so adding 22 rows did not WEAKEN either clause** -- which is the thing a closure that grows an instrument has to show and usually does not.  *A larger detector can dilute a clause without anyone noticing: the same absolute kill count against a bigger denominator reads as a higher score.  Here the pre-fix and reinstatement legs are still 49 rows short of BASE.*

*** 2026-09-11 CLASS-CLOSURE REVIEW (codex GPT-6 Astra at max).  **THE CLASS CLOSURE I DEMANDED IS NOT ESTABLISHED, AND FOUR OF MY PREMISES WERE WRONG.** ***

*VERDICT: The declined PUT repair is correct as written; the claimed complete class closure is not established.  A separate buffer-initialization defect remains in the worktree.*

**THE REPAIR ITSELF STANDS.**  What is refused is the framing I put around it.

=== FOUR PREMISE CORRECTIONS, each checkable ===
  1. **The probe is already past the 59-row instrument I quoted.**  It carries the pass-4 nibble and coordinate additions; statically expanding its loops gives **77 assertions in 17 sessions** -- four earlier assertions removed, 22 added.  *I was reasoning about a detector two passes stale.*
  2. *** THE SIX ESCAPES ARE NOT SIX POSITION-SELECTOR ESCAPES, and my own table had FIVE entries. ***  The probe names them **M28, M30, M31, M32, M33 and M37** -- and describes **M28 as a COLOUR-NIBBLE mutant and M37 as a FOREGROUND-VALUE mutant.**  *So the 'one class, six instances' story that triggered my class-closure demand is itself wrong: at most four are position selectors.*
  3. **There is no shared executable tail after this function's PUT/GET branches** -- the function ends immediately after them.  *The common-tail restriction I cited belongs to a DIFFERENT function, `DEVICE_ACCESS(sgi_re)`.*
  4. **`63 68 69 6e` spells "chin" and that does not establish provenance.**  *'The security-relevant evidence is the transfer of uninitialized automatic storage across the guest boundary.  Printable content is neither necessary nor sufficient to prove that provenance.'*  **I had used the recognisable string as if it were the proof.**

=== *** THE DOCTRINAL KEY IS IN THE PARTITION TABLE, AND IT DISSOLVES MY FLOOR CLAIM *** ===
The seat enumerated what the body ACTUALLY TESTS, distinguishing *a value being tested* from *a value contributing to an operand*:

| lvalue | partition the BODY induces |
|---|---|
| `put` | zero / nonzero |
| `tlb_mode` | switch labels 0,1,2,4,default; other tests split default's 3 from 5-7 |
| `linear` | derived from `tlb_mode > 3` -- **NOT an independent axis** |
| incoming `x`, `y` | `< 0` / in-range / `>= 2048` where evaluated.  **There is no `x == 0` or `y == 0` test**, and a later `y &= 127` changes the value a mutant sees |
| tiled `tile_nr` | `< 256` / `>= 256`.  *** NO ZERO/NONZERO TEST EXISTS *** |
| linear `tile_nr` | `< 32` / `>= 32` **after reassignment `tile_nr = x >> 12` -- a DIFFERENT value from the tiled calculation** |
| `color_mode` | CI / RGB / RGBA / ABGR / default, where **default is twelve NIBBLE VALUES, not twelve switch labels** |

> *** BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30`'s `if (tile_nr == 0) ok = 0;` IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT. ***  *My brief demanded closure over selectors the rule does not put inside the floor, which is the `#392` shape wearing the class-closure rule's clothes.  The seat's closing sentence is the one to keep: these additions **'must not be represented as full closure over arbitrary predicates on all function inputs.'***

=== THE BOUNDED, REVIEWABLE IMPROVEMENT -- what is actually owed ===
  * **eleven missing mode/depth/latch cells**;
  * **one reverse-latch assertion** -- one aggregate `colour/others` assertion appended to an EXISTING colour-first session: after the colour announcement, drive the twelve other sites and require each expected announcement.  **Control family `SET_OTHER(j)`: the colour warning update also sets another site's bit**, observable as the missing announcement from site `j`.  *The current other-first sequence stays green under that error because the other bit was already set.*  **One assertion, no new process.**
  * **strengthened four depth-eight assertions**;
  * an **unconditional default-arm `return`**;
  * a **contract that names its ACTUAL partitions**.

*** A CAUTION ON EXTENDING COORDINATES, which would have bitten the obvious implementation: *** *'Reusing C1's fixed vertex at another depth can select another tile; changing only the mode can turn a proposed decline test into an earlier invalid-pointer return.'*  **Each added address/depth setup needs an ACCEPTING control proving that mapping reaches its intended destination** -- otherwise a row that looks like a decline test is really an early-return test.

=== `buf[8] = {0}` IS ACCEPTED, BUT NOT AS BELT-AND-BRACES ===
**Accepted as a candidate companion repair on a TRANSFERRED WARRANT**: the same file's `#509` comment records the same buffer-to-guest failure mechanism and explicitly leaves other widths outstanding.  **Not a measured delta.**  And it is not free -- *'I would not describe it as merely belt-and-braces'*:
  * **it changes six accepted PUT format/depth combinations**;
  * at the shared declaration it **also changes GET behaviour when the read supplies fewer bytes than packing consumes**;
  * it establishes deterministic bytes, **not hardware-correct semantics** for every unsupported combination;
  * its generated-code and performance cost are unmeasured.

*'The permitted files do not establish that zero padding is the intended hardware behavior for all those combinations.  They do establish why copying uninitialized storage is unacceptable.'*

**AND THE TWO ROWS STAY SEPARATE, with the invariants named:** [[sgirandomcolour]] = *an unsupported PUT performs NO STORE*; [[sgirebufuninit]] = *every byte consumed by an actual transfer or colour reconstruction is INITIALIZED*.  **Different invariants, so the distinction survives** -- I had asked whether the six escapes collapse them, and they do not.

**STATUS: `#519` still must not commit as-is** (the escapes are real and the default arm should return unconditionally), **but the round owes a BOUNDED list, not the unbounded closure I specified.**  Landing held by owner ruling.

